    {
      "text": "Son of man is Lord even of the sabbath, Matt. 12:8 (Mark 2:28; Luke 6:5). lawful to heal on the sabbath, Matt. 12:10 (Mark 3:2; Luke 6:7). lawful to do well on the sabbath, Matt. 12:12 (Mark 3:4; Luke 6:9). flight be not in the winter, neither on the sabbath, Matt. 24:20. end of the sabbath, as it began to dawn, Matt. 28:1 (Luke 4:31). sabbath was made for man, and not man for the sabbath, Mark 2:27. be loosed from this bond on the sabbath, Luke 13:16. fallen into a pit … pull him out on the sabbath, Luke 14:5. they … rested the sabbath day according to the commandment, Luke 23:56. sabbath … not lawful for thee to carry thy bed, John 5:10. man on the sabbath day receive circumcision, John 7:23. sabbath day when Jesus made the clay, John 9:14. should not remain upon the cross on the sabbath, John 19:31. first day of the week cometh Mary Magdalene, John 20:1. Gentiles besought that these words might be preached to them the next sabbath, Acts 13:42. reasoned in the synagogue every sabbath, Acts 18:4. first day of the week … Paul preached, Acts 20:7. first day of the week let every one of you lay by him in store, 1 Cor. 16:2. Let no man therefore judge you … in respect of … sabbath days, Col. 2:16. spake in a certain place of the seventh day, Heb. 4:4. I was in the Spirit on the Lord’s day, Rev. 1:10.",
